# DESK18 -- launch C:\SUB\CURDIR.NCP from the LEFT window.
#
# Three clicks, not two: the AES gives a click on a window that is not the top
# one to the owner as WM_TOPPED and swallows it (EmuTOS `hctl_window`,
# `aes/gemctrl.c:172-179`; our AES does the same -- run a's first attempt,
# `[aes] ... op 25 ... out=(16,...)` = MU_MESAG). So the first click tops
# C:\SUB\, and the double-click that follows opens the program.
#
# Click point (47, 92) = CURDIR.NCP's icon-glyph centre from the probe dump
# (`[desk18]   obj 12 'CURDIR.NCP' box (9,76) 76x40 -> click (47,92)`).
100 parkbr
300 move 600 460
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 47 92
1800 down
1803 up
2400 mark B_TOPPED
2700 down
2703 up
2708 down
2711 up
